From d938b21c0ca2e7cc3e85a35c3fdd943a738dbf20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Warburton <tyler@cipherplay.net>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:21:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] timelock@1.0: one RSA-2048 group, commit g^alpha, sound
 Wesolowski cracks

Port the device to RandAO's new time-lock protocol (SPEC 2.3, 2.5, 3).
The per-validator modulus is gone: N is the built-in RSA-2048 challenge
number, g is derived from "rng/timelock/g" and cached with the small
primes in a persistent term.

- generator: returns g and n.
- verify-reveal (c, alpha, h): 0 < c, h < N, alpha at most 512 bits,
  g^alpha = c; returns canonical(h^alpha).
- verify-crack (x, t, y, proof): 0 < x, y, proof < N, t =< 2^32;
  challenge hash no longer includes N; returns canonical(y).
- derive-x and the p reveal are removed; verify-bls and derive unchanged.
- Hex inputs capped at 512 digits (alpha at 128).
- New reference vectors (36 cases, T = 1024), docs and PARALITH.md row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
